.TH 7ZZ 1 "2026-09-03" "7-Zip 26.03" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
7zz \- 7-Zip file archiver, console version
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B 7zz
.I <command>
.RI [ <switches> ...]
.I <archive_name>
.RI [ <file_names> ...]
.RI [ @listfile ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B 7zz
is the command line version of 7\-Zip, a file archiver with a high
compression ratio.  It reads and writes the 7z format and can also
read many other archive formats, including ZIP, RAR, TAR, GZIP, BZIP2,
XZ, CAB, ISO, DMG, APFS, NTFS, WIM, VHD/VHDX/VMDI/VDI, SquashFS and
several filesystem images.
.PP
This manual page documents the
.B 7zz
binary installed by this package.  The authoritative documentation for
the command syntax and the 7z format is installed under
.IR /usr/local/share/doc/7\-Zip/ .
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B a
Add files to archive.
.TP
.B b
Benchmark: measure compression and decompression speed.
.TP
.B d
Delete files from archive.
.TP
.B e
Extract files from archive, without restoring directory names.
.TP
.B h
Calculate hash values for files.
.TP
.B i
Show information about supported formats, codecs and hashers.
.TP
.B l
List contents of archive.
.TP
.B rn
Rename files in archive.
.TP
.B t
Test integrity of archive.
.TP
.B u
Update files to archive.
.TP
.B x
Extract files with full paths.
.SH SWITCHES
.TP
.B \-o{Directory}
Set the output directory for extracted files.
.TP
.B \-p{Password}
Set a password.  Use
.B \-p
with no value to be prompted interactively.
.TP
.B \-m{Parameters}
Set the compression method, for example
.BR \-mx=9
for maximum compression or
.BR \-m0=lzma2
to select the codec explicitly.
.TP
.B \-t{Type}
Set the archive type, for example
.BR \-t7z " or " \-tzip .
.TP
.B \-y
Assume
.B yes
on all queries.
.TP
.B \-r[\-|0]
Recurse subdirectories for name search.
.TP
.B \-v{Size}[b|k|m|g]
Create multi\-volume archive with the given volume size.
.TP
.B \-si[{name}]
Read data from standard input.
.TP
.B \-so
Write data to standard output.
.TP
.B \-slt
Show technical information for the
.B l
command.
.TP
.B \-scrc{CRC32|CRC64|SHA256|SHA1|XXH64|BLAKE2SP|*}
Set the hash function used by the
.BR x ,
.B e
and
.B h
commands.
.TP
.B \-sdel
Delete files after they have been compressed.
.TP
.B \-snl
Store symbolic links as links instead of following them.
.TP
.B \-snh
Store hard links as links.
.TP
.B \-ssw
Compress shared files.
.TP
.B \-ssp
Do not change the last access time of source files while archiving.
.TP
.B \-bb[0\-3]
Set the output log level.
.TP
.B \-bd
Disable the progress indicator.
.TP
.B \-spd
Disable wildcard matching for file names.
.TP
.B \-w[{path}]
Assign a working directory.  An empty path selects a temporary directory.
.TP
.B \-x[r[\-|0]][m[\-|2]][w[\-]]{@listfile|!wildcard}
Exclude file names.
.TP
.B \-i[r[\-|0]][m[\-|2]][w[\-]]{@listfile|!wildcard}
Include file names.
.SH EXAMPLES
Create a maximum\-compression 7z archive:
.PP
.RS 4
.B 7zz a \-t7z \-mx=9 archive.7z dir/
.RE
.PP
List an archive with technical details:
.PP
.RS 4
.B 7zz l \-slt archive.7z
.RE
.PP
Extract to a specific directory, answering yes to all prompts:
.PP
.RS 4
.B 7zz x archive.7z \-o/tmp/dest \-y
.RE
.PP
Verify archive integrity:
.PP
.RS 4
.B 7zz t archive.7z
.RE
.PP
Create an encrypted archive (AES\-256):
.PP
.RS 4
.B 7zz a \-p archive.7z secret.txt
.RE
.PP
Stream a tar archive to standard output:
.PP
.RS 4
.B 7zz a \-ttar \-so dir/ | gzip > dir.tar.gz
.RE
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/local/bin/7zz
The executable.
.TP
.I /usr/local/bin/7z
Convenience symbolic link to
.IR 7zz .
.TP
